{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"589a14793c4f88a1","name":"card_event_uss_missouri","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_uss_missouri","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"USS MISSOURI","text":"Destroy target unit in the frontline. Retreat adjacent units.","flavorText":"The USS Missouri (BB-63) was the last battleship commissioned by the US Navy during WWII. She played a significant role in the Pacific Theater. Launched in January 1944, she was armed with nine 406mm (16-inch) main guns capable of striking targets over 32 kilometers away, along with twenty 127mm (5-inch) secondary guns and numerous anti-aircraft weapons. This powerful armament made her a formidable force in shore bombardments and fleet defense. After her launch, Missouri joined the Pacific Theater, where she provided anti-aircraft cover and naval gunfire support during major operations, including the Battles of Iwo Jima and Okinawa. Her most iconic moment came on September 2, 1945, when she hosted the formal Japanese surrender ceremony in Tokyo Bay, officially ending WWII. Representatives of the Allied Powers, led by General Douglas MacArthur, and the Empire of Japan signed the surrender on her deck. Although she would serve in later conflicts, Missouri’s legacy is most closely tied to her role in the final chapter of WWII. Today, she is preserved as a museum ship at Pearl Harbor.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"GameplayTags":["subtype.navy"],"Name":"card_event_uss_missouri","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_uss_missouri_title","SourceString":"USS MISSOURI","LocalizedString":"USS MISSOURI"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_uss_missouri_text","SourceString":"Destroy target unit in the frontline. Retreat adjacent units.","LocalizedString":"Dest